  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS DRC 2024 &#x2013; UNICEF WASH Emergency Specialist</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an assignment at the request of UNICEF. Since March 2022, fighting between local armed groups in the Rutshuru, Nyiragongo and Masisi regions in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) has forced large numbers of civilians to flee their homes. More than 2.5 million people have been internally displaced in North Kivu. Since the beginning of January 2024, fighting between armed groups has spread to several regions, leading to large-scale internal displacement. More than 72,000 displaced people are living in extremely dangerous conditions due to overcrowding caused by the influx of newly displaced people to villages along the Sake-Bweremana axis. To this end, the WASH sector requires an experienced WASH specialist to support the UNICEF Goma office WASH team to ensure quality and timely humanitarian response in the North Kivu.</narrative>
  </description>
